# The network of "Write why-not": the office's network, with a server and
# a router on it, and a back-office network behind the router.
#
#   office 10.0.7.10 --+
#   srv    10.0.7.20 --[shop]-- r1 10.0.7.1 / 10.0.9.1 --[back]-- far 10.0.9.30
#
# srv and far each run a web server on port 80 and a firewall
# (/etc/nftables.conf) that drops ping and two ports. Nothing in the lab
# owns 10.0.7.200 to 10.0.7.249. The checks plug throwaway machines of
# their own into the two switches, at 10.0.7.100 to 149 and 10.0.9.100 to
# 149, with ports of their own choosing.
machine office
machine srv
machine r1 router
machine far

lan shop office:eth0=10.0.7.10/24 srv:eth0=10.0.7.20/24 r1:eth0=10.0.7.1/24
lan back r1:eth1=10.0.9.1/24 far:eth0=10.0.9.30/24

route office default via 10.0.7.1
route srv default via 10.0.7.1
route far default via 10.0.9.1

run srv nginx nftables
run far nginx nftables
